{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Six days.</b> So it is written at the first." "<b>And the sense of \"in plowing and in harvest.\"</b> That they are the essence of human life. Anan, may his name be blotted out, said like Anan [?], for this concerns lying with a woman — and indeed let shame cover it. For if we say that plowing is in the hand of the man, then with the word \"harvest\" he would plow [i.e., the word קציר itself alludes to plowing]." "And he did not mention the year of Shemittah in this section, because the known complete day is the movement of the uppermost sphere from east to west in twenty-four hours, and the solar year is three hundred and sixty-five days and nearly a quarter of a day, for it is the cycle of the sun from its beginning until it returns to its place — and the scholars of the stars will understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {1 "The text כענן כי is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The reference is to Anan ben David, founder of Karaism; Ibn Ezra's syntax here is compressed and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:26.615358941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}